-- Wiebe's theorem (ctete Theorem 11).  The step (WiebeCore.Step) reads
-- memberships "x in (J, b)" through cat (the last generator split off by
-- Plus), whose elements are merely coordinates (Generated.In, Trunc);
-- Fin/Vec/Mat/plus/extend/snoc decode the lists.  The induction opens its
-- own statement (Thm, Goal, Delta, Concl), the generic change its own (Gen,
-- Out), and the rings RD/ext1 at instances; no proof body is opened.
-- K, T, bt, at, Goal are the step's names for (J, b_<), (J, b, a), b_n,
-- a_n and its conclusion; Cong/sub is "x = y mod (K)".
WiebeCore.Over.Step.perp: Perp In cat extend snoc plus Generated.In TrueGradeIdeals.Over.In carrier image D Cong sub Plus.K K T bt
WiebeCore.Over.Step.ann: Ann In cat extend snoc plus Fin Vec Generated.In TrueGradeIdeals.Over.In carrier image D Cong sub Plus.K K bt at Goal
WiebeCore.Over.Step.result: Concl
WiebeGeneric.GenStep.result: RD In Generated.In TrueGradeIdeals.Over.In
WiebeGeneric.generic: RD Gen
Wiebe.Induction.result: Hom RD Gen
Wiebe.Induction.After.result: Fin carrier image Generated.In RD TrueGradeIdeals.Over.In In
Wiebe.theorem11: RD Vec Mat Delta Thm Concl Goal
